        "**CONCLUSION:**\n",
        "\n",
        "The demand recovery significantly improves forecasting performance when an effective recovery model is employed. Among all evaluated approaches, DLinear-based recovery achieved the lowest WAPE (0.2185), outperforming both heuristic recovery methods and the censored-data baseline. Compared with the baseline model trained directly on censored sales data, DLinear reduced forecasting error by approximately 12.6%, indicating that the recovered demand contains valuable information that was not captured in the observed sales alone. Furthermore, improvements were observed across both low-sale and high-sale product groups, suggesting that the learned recovery model was able to reconstruct meaningful demand patterns rather than introducing additional noise."
